  "course_description": "This course is designed to give advanced students the opportunity to investigate intensively a specialized topic in film and media studies. May be repeated for credit when topic varies.",
  "course_notes": "This course explores the true crime genre in film, print, and popular media such as television, streaming platforms, YouTube, and podcasts. In addition to surveying the history and enduring popularity of true crime, the course investigates the cultural fascination with crime and criminals behind the genre¿s prevalence and profitability; the role, construction, and presentation of truth in nonfiction film, literature, and media; and questions of responsibility, exploitation, and victimhood that shape what has been called the ¿true crime industrial complex.¿",
